/P 117 0 R
/E (The methodology of this project is based on modeling the organ matching process as a structured search problem. Initially, the system defines the state space where each state represents a donor-recipient pair. The initial state consists of all available donors and recipients. Actions are defined as selecting a donor and matching them with a compatible recipient. The transition model is clearly structured, where the system moves from one state to another by selecting valid donor-recipient pairs that satisfy compatibility constraints. )
/Pg 22 0 R
/K [3]
>>
